// A List built-in method is not a value: a read of `l.pop` that is not a
// direct call is a halting fault (spec/04-semantics.md, Property Get step 6
// and Halting Faults). A direct call `l.pop()` still runs, and so do
// `l.append(x)` and `l.remove(x)`.
var l = [1, 2, 3];
l.append(4);
print l.pop();
l.remove(1);
print l;
print l.pop;
print "unreachable";

// STATUS: error
// CHECK: 4
// CHECK: [2, 3]
